1. Script create karo
cat > /usr/local/bin/check_ip_forward.sh <<'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

FILE="/etc/sysctl.conf"

if grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*net\.ipv4\.ip_forward[[:space:]]*=' "$FILE"; then
    sed -i -E 's/^[[:space:]]*net\.ipv4\.ip_forward[[:space:]]*=.*/net.ipv4.ip_forward = 0/' "$FILE"
else
    echo "net.ipv4.ip_forward = 0" >> "$FILE"
fi

sysctl --system
EOF

chmod 755 /usr/local/bin/check_ip_forward.sh
2. Reboot ke baad automatically run karne ke liye service
cat > /etc/systemd/system/check-ip-forward.service <<'EOF'
[Unit]
Description=Ensure net.ipv4.ip_forward is set to 0
After=systemd-sysctl.service
Before=multi-user.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/check_ip_forward.sh

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
EOF
3. Enable karo
systemctl daemon-reload && systemctl enable check-ip-forward.service
Ab har reboot ke baad service automatically:
/etc/sysctl.conf check karegi
net.ipv4.ip_forward ko 0 karegi
sysctl --system run karegi
Check
systemctl status check-ip-forward.service
sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward
grep "net.ipv4.ip_forward" /etc/sysctl.conf
Expected:
net.ipv4.ip_forward = 0
Important: Ye /etc/sysctl.conf ko correct karega. Agar kisi aur file, jaise /etc/sysctl.d/*.conf, mein ip_forward=1 configured hai, to woh later override kar sakti hai. Agar aap chaho to main aapko �⁠ek single script de sakta hoon jo reboot ke baad poore `/etc/sysctl.d/` ko bhi check karke automatically `0` enforce kare.